From 63ec9fcb45cb0cf59214a3d2b676f408d724cf62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MT6762 local experiment <mt6762-build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:06:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm: add explicit PMIC thermal conversion laboratory fixtures

AI-assisted local experiment, not intended for upstream submission. Thermal fixtures default off and use explicitly synthetic calibration, timed READY transitions, per-channel counters and scoped faults. No phone temperature measurement, CPU thermal freshness, DVFS or control policy is claimed.
---
 docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst        |  24 +++++++
 hw/arm/mt6762.c                   |  27 +++++++-
 hw/arm/mt6762_lab_power.c         |  73 ++++++++++++++++++----
 include/hw/arm/mt6762_lab_power.h |   7 +++
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_power.py    |   5 +-
 tests/mt6762/test_lab_thermal.py  | 100 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 220 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/mt6762/test_lab_thermal.py

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
index 579dca0..2253e9c 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/mt6762.rst
@@ -222,3 +222,27 @@ release, rejected malformed setters and restoration of default behavior.
 The source-only XNU helper ``touch_lab.py`` waits for two completed native
 DMA reads after each published frame before advancing a gesture. Model
 counters still represent synthetic I2C traffic, not real touch hardware.
+
+Explicit synthetic PMIC thermal conversions
+-------------------------------------------
+
+``lab-pmic-thermal=on`` requires ``lab-power=on`` and separately enables
+synthetic calibrated PMIC die/VCORE/VPROC ADC registers. Without it those
+thermal fixtures remain absent. The fixed efuse data is invented test data,
+never a calibration recovered from this phone. No CPU thermal controller,
+CPU freshness guarantee, thermal policy, rail control or DVFS is emulated.
+
+Each channel clears READY on its request and raises it after80 virtual us.
+A native consumer must establish READY-low then READY-high before accepting
+a sample. ``thermal-timeout``, ``thermal-stale``, ``thermal-uncalibrated``,
+``thermal-bad-degc``, ``thermal-mux`` and ``thermal-rail`` extend the
+``lab-power-fault`` values. The mux fault affects only the die/CH4 route;
+buck conversions are independent. Battery/NTC conversions remain separate.
+``lab-power-state`` records thermal enablement, synthetic calibration and
+per-channel request/completion counters.
+
+``tests/mt6762/test_lab_thermal.py`` tests conversion transitions, faults,
+ADC isolation and default absence. Native ``--native-lab-thermal`` separately
+asserts ``pmic-thermal-adc-owned``. Host scheduling may let a short conversion
+finish before the guest observes READY-low; conservative guest rejection is
+expected and must not be reported as a valid fresh sample.
